      "content": "interesting. you're saying their concerns are basically just \"short-term convenience.\" \n\nbut if i'm presenting this to a municipal board, i'm going to get grilled on the actual economics. how do i counter the argument that highways are objectively more cost-effective for freight and moving goods compared to rail, which can be incredibly slow and expensive to implement? \n\ni want to make it sound like the 'cost-effective' argument is actually a false premise. how would you frame that?",
